Package: banff
Title: R Interface to the 'Banff' Statistical Data Editing Procedures
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Colin", "Weaver", email = "colingweaver@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Calls the nine 'Banff' procedures (Statistics Canada) for statistical data
    editing and imputation (verifyedits, editstats, outlier, errorloc, deterministic,
    donorimp, estimator, prorate, massimp) from R. By default calls the official Banff C
    libraries directly via the Arrow C data interface (no Python needed); can also go
    through the Python 'banff' package with 'reticulate'.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 8.1.1
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    nanoarrow (>= 0.5),
    tibble
Suggests:
    bench,
    DBI,
    duckdb,
    reticulate,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
